Chapter: Shared

 Shared memory primitives for GPU kernels. Shared memory is a
 fast, block-scoped scratch space visible to all threads in a
 thread block. SharedArray has a compile-time-known size;
 DynamicSharedArray is sized at launch via lc-shared-bytes.

 We say:

Section: Types

  SharedArray = record {
    sa-base : Integer,
    sa-count : Integer
  }

  DynamicSharedArray = record {
    dsa-base : Integer
  }

Section: Construction

  make-shared-array : Integer, Integer -> SharedArray
  make-shared-array (base) (count) =
    SharedArray { sa-base = base, sa-count = count }

  make-dynamic-shared : Integer -> DynamicSharedArray
  make-dynamic-shared (base) = DynamicSharedArray { dsa-base = base }

